[TEXT] Excellent — **anomaly found immediately on router0**. The routing table reveals the "temporary backup route":

```
1.0.0.0/8 via 127.0.0.1 dev lo   ← manually injected static route pointing to loopback!
```

All other routers have correct RIP-learned routes. Router0 should have `1.0.0.0/8 via 10.10.0.2 dev eth2` (like its other remote routes), but instead 1.0.0.0/8 traffic is being sent to `127.0.0.1` on loopback — a blackhole. Internet (128.168.0.0/16) still goes correctly via `10.10.0.2 eth2`.

Let me confirm the symptom end-to-end from an IT host:
