=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: router0
diagnosis_text:
**Affected component:** A manually injected static route on router0 for the Server Room subnet (`1.0.0.0/8`), pointing its next-hop to the loopback address `127.0.0.1 dev lo`.

**Mechanism:** When IT or CS hosts (subnets 192.168.1.0/24 and 192.168.2.0/24) send packets to the Server Room (1.0.0.x), those packets transit router0. Router0 looks up its routing table, matches the static route `1.0.0.0/8 via 127.0.0.1 dev lo` (which was incorrectly added by the admin as a "temporary backup route"), and forwards them to its own loopback interface. The kernel re-injects the packet, hits the same route, and creates a tight routing loop on router0 until the IP TTL reaches zero. Router0 then sends an ICMP "Time to live exceeded" back to the sender — confirmed live by `ping` from `it_hod`, which shows 100% loss with TTL-exceeded errors sourced from 192.168.1.1 (router0's LAN-IT interface).

**Why Internet Lab still works:** The Internet route (`128.168.0.0/16 via 10.10.0.2 dev eth2`) is a valid RIP-learned route unaffected by the bad static entry. Packets to 128.168.0.x are forwarded correctly over the WAN link to router1 → router2.

**Localization:** Solely router0. Router1 and router2 carry correct RIP routes for `1.0.0.0/8`.

**Root cause:** An admin-added static route `1.0.0.0/8 via 127.0.0.1 dev lo` on router0 blackholes and micro-loops all traffic destined for the Server Room.

**Fix:** Remove the bad route on router0: `ip route del 1.0.0.0/8 via 127.0.0.1 dev lo`. The correct RIP-learned route will then be reinstated automatically.
=== END ===